Subject: animate a program's redraw that moves its rows, as a region scroll

smooth-scroll animates a region scroll the terminal is told about
(DECSTBM with SU/SD, IND/RI at a margin). Many full-screen programs move
their content by repainting every row instead: pi's full-screen view
rewrites each changed row in place, in one synchronized update, for every
streamed line and every wheel step, so the terminal never sees a scroll and
the content jumps a row at a time. On the alternate screen, when the
terminal recorded no scroll, the renderer now compares each row's hash with
the previous frame's: when at least half of the rows that changed (and at
least three) are the old ones moved by the same number of rows, that span,
between rows that stayed as they were (a header, a prompt), is animated
exactly as a region scroll of it, ghost rows and hit testing included.

Calm's own patch (not from thdxg/ghostty); applies on top of 0005 and 0008.

